Example: cash deposits change the balance without creating investment profit.
The only selected holding is Assets:Cash. Salary of 100 USD on 2023-01-01 and
a 50 USD bonus on 2023-07-01 leave 150 USD at the end of the year-long report.
Opening value is 0, net contributions are 100 + 50 = 150 USD, and profit/loss
is ending value 150 - opening value 0 - contributions 150 = 0 USD.
The value never grows apart from deposits, so both return measures are 0%.
The ending 150 USD exactly repays the two deposits, regardless of their dates.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight investment-performance --accounts Assets:Cash --commodities USD --from 2023-01-01 --to 2024-01-01 --format text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
account Assets:Cash
account Income:Salary
account Income:Bonus

2023-01-01 Salary
  Assets:Cash  100 USD
  Income:Salary  -100 USD

2023-07-01 Bonus
  Assets:Cash  50 USD
  Income:Bonus  -50 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2023-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 0.00 USD
Net contributions: 150.00 USD
Ending value: 150.00 USD
Profit/loss: 0.00 USD
Time-weighted return: 0.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): 0.00 %
Money-weighted return (annualized): 0.00 %

========== WARNINGS ==========
